      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this replaces the local minimums obtained previously from the idle and active CPUs, with a global minimum for the non-prefer idle case. Everything higher in either case B and C will be filtered out. This fixes the scenario in which we have all LITTLE CPUs idle and all bigs active, when we\u0027d chose a big CPU as target_cpu and a LITTLE idle CPU as backup idle CPU. \"energy_diff\" might choose the big active one as it will only compare against the previous CPUs, and not consider backup as well (depending on FBT_STRICT_ORDER).",
